{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The discipline of a father</b> — that his father would discipline him, for he knows that he will accept discipline when he is wise." "<b>And a scorner's son</b> — he will not hear his father's rebuke, for he does not wish to discipline him because of his scorning, and he knows that he will not accept it; or he will not be willing to hear the one who would discipline him."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:28.216269713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}